# Draft: asahi: add support for interchange_compressed
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/39755 state=closed
# Apple hardware also supports the compressed "interchange" tile format.

Buffers of this format are to be only used for scanout,
i.e. for interchange between different system components. Accordingly,
this format will only be used when the corresponding drm modifier
is specified.

When uploading a texture descriptor for such a buffer, the layer count
must be set to `ceil(width/16)`, even though the texture is
logically 2D.

As a result, only textures with depth 1 are supported (no array textures).


Works together with this kernel change:
https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux/pull/449
